-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN: the main build (stable line, ~/.cache/l4-main/112) gives a different class on five of the 35 traces; the unstable build (20261125-a50cbd0) matches every EXPECT.
-- The five are the traces in which nobody applies to the Court and the last day for applying (day 89) passes, so the power of the creditor, member or person owed an obligation lapses:
--   1. "Nobody applies to the Court, and the window closed on day 89, before the last step" (s 215 chain from the resolution, long form): expected FULFILLED; main reads RESIDUAL, the Court's four alternatives (paragraphs (a), (b), (c) and any other order) shown as still open.
--   2. "The amalgamated company is a new company: the Registrar issues the notice with the notice of incorporation": expected FULFILLED; main reads RESIDUAL for the same reason.
--   3. "The short form: the members resolve under section 215D(1) on day 59 ... the Court is not applied to": expected FULFILLED; main reads RESIDUAL for the same reason.
--   4. "The existing gate of section 215D(2), all six conditions met" (whole chain, short form): expected FULFILLED; main reads RESIDUAL for the same reason.
--   5. "The gate of section 215D(2) fails on one condition" (whole chain, long form): expected FULFILLED; main reads RESIDUAL for the same reason.
-- Every trace in which an application to the Court is made in time, and the trace in which the application is made on the date of effect, reads the same on both builds.
